  "adaptations": [
    "Imports use MAIN namespaces, token/Clock/loader/RPC/authority/hash primitives and the single eplyx lifecycle command tree. Explicit inputs replace issuer-specific CLI defaults.",
    "Wide integers and Scaled UI multiplier bits use MAIN serialization. Original frozen bytes remain untouched; the encoding-projection manifest enumerates file and internal digest changes. Every economic value and result remains unchanged.",
    "Known Blocked and Incomplete readiness map to MAIN exits 1 and 5. JSON aborts use MAIN error objects instead of empty stdout/stderr-only errors. Output protection and the original error reasons remain asserted.",
    "The scenario-mismatch negative test changes identifying policy rather than its display description, which MAIN intentionally excludes from identity.",
    "Tampering tests operate on independent scratch packages with valid bounded relative paths, so they exercise digest and fresh-execution rejection rather than failing early on absolute references.",
    "Historical artifact preservation is checked for every imported original byte against both its source inventory and the original phase-14 checksum when listed. The archive-wide source preservation assertion is checked by the phase audit of all 1633 inventoried STA files; unrelated archive files are not copied into MAIN.",
    "The old Phase 6 standalone coverage command remains archived per scope; its 15 reusable coverage assertions are retained. Source expansion capture/discovery products are not exposed by the lifecycle CLI.",
    "Clock copies use the shared Copy type, with no source behavior change. Source support diagnostics retain their assertions while provider origin uses a fixed non-secret acquisition label.",
    "The guard transports the parent host temporary root explicitly to the empty-environment worker, preserving the source temporary-marker restriction on macOS. Source negative guard exit values use MAIN mapping.",
    "Position and token-transfer unit tests run in T6 because lifecycle assurance depends on those executors; T7 adds the complete current-path integration surface and remaining probe/position suites."
  ],
  "additional_checks": [
    "lifecycle kind has no executable, upgrade target or delivery",
    "all declared semantic terms identify the change; metadata and absent optional fields do not",
    "complete field provenance and canonical address/hash validation",
    "bound lifecycle CLI reports are byte-identical over repeated inputs",
    "parent fake credential sentinels do not reach offline evaluation; direct inherited environment is rejected",
    "server lifecycle run indexing contains asset identity without candidate fields",
    "wide scores preserve u128/i128 extremes and reject lossy numeric inputs",
    "artifact byte bounds, package escape and symlink rejection",
    "full generated notice impact equals the independently projected pinned impact",
    "floating-point source guard covers every newly migrated analytical module"
  ]
